    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1178fa19-d93c-5872-93dd-368134c3546d",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]$ at $t=\\frac{\\pi}{12}$ given that $∇f(x,y)=\\left(- 4 y \\sin{\\left(x y \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(- 4 x \\sin{\\left(x y \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}$ and $\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\left(3 \\sqrt{t}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(- 2 \\sqrt{t}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]=∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nIn addition, we've been given that\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\left(- 4 y \\sin{\\left(x y \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(- 4 x \\sin{\\left(x y \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we substitute $x=3 \\sqrt{t}$ and $y=- 2 \\sqrt{t}$ into $∇f(x,y)$ to find $∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =\\left(- 4 y \\sin{\\left(x y \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(- 4 x \\sin{\\left(x y \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\Big|_{x=3 \\sqrt{t},\\,y=- 2 \\sqrt{t}} \\\\  & =\\left(- 8 \\sqrt{t} \\sin{\\left(6 t \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(12 \\sqrt{t} \\sin{\\left(6 t \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $\\mathbf{r}(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(3 \\sqrt{t}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(- 2 \\sqrt{t}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{3}{2 \\sqrt{t}}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(- \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))] & =∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(- 8 \\sqrt{t} \\sin{\\left(6 t \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(12 \\sqrt{t} \\sin{\\left(6 t \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\left(\\frac{3}{2 \\sqrt{t}}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(- \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(- 8 \\sqrt{t} \\sin{\\left(6 t \\right)}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{3}{2 \\sqrt{t}}\\right)+\\left(12 \\sqrt{t} \\sin{\\left(6 t \\right)}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(- 12 \\sin{\\left(6 t \\right)}\\right)+\\left(- 12 \\sin{\\left(6 t \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =- 24 \\sin{\\left(6 t \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the above at $t=\\frac{\\pi}{12},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]\\Big|_{t=\\frac{\\pi}{12}} & =- 24 \\sin{\\left(6 t \\right)}\\Big|_{t=\\frac{\\pi}{12}} \\\\  & =\\left(-12\\right)+\\left(-12\\right) \\\\  & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
